LID - 10.1055/s-0043-125092 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has revolutionized the diagnosis of lung cancer 
      over the last decade. This minimally invasive diagnostic method has also become 
      increasingly important in the case of other diseases such as sarcoidosis, thereby 
      helping to avoid unnecessary diagnostic interventions. This review article 
      provides an update regarding EBUS and discusses current and future developments 
      of this method.
