TI  - EBUS-TBNA for Diagnosis of Extrapulmonary Lesions.
PG  - 59-60
LID - 10.4103/JOC.JOC_124_18 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) has 
      recently emerged as a minimally invasive and safe modality for the evaluation of 
      mediastinal lymphadenopathy, particularly in staging of lung carcinoma patients. 
      In high tuberculosis endemic countries, EBUS-TBNA is useful in obtaining tissue 
      diagnosis of granulomatous inflammation. Role of EBUS-TBNA in workup of 
      extrapulmonary malignancies is not widely described. Herein, a brief overview of 
      importance of EBUS-TBNA in investigation of extrapulmonary lesions/malignancies 
      is presented.
