TI  - Contrast-enhanced endobronchial ultrasound: Potential value of a new method.
PG  - 43-48
LID - 10.4103/2303-9027.200215 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has gained importance for mediastinal lymph node 
      staging. Contrast-enhanced EBUS is so far not a discussed technique including 
      contrast-enhanced high mechanical index (MI)-EBUS and potentially 
      contrast-enhanced low MI-EBUS. Possible use could include characterization of 
      mediastinal lymph nodes for better selection of biopsies, differential diagnosis 
      of the primary tumor, and evaluation of thrombosis or tumor in vein infiltration.
