TI  - The vanishing lesion: A procedural clue to pneumothorax during endobronchial 
      ultrasound.
PG  - 211-213
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_640_25 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has become an essential tool in lung cancer 
      staging and the diagnosis of centrally located pulmonary lesions. Vigilance 
      during EBUS-guided biopsy is crucial. The disappearance of a previously 
      visualised lesion should raise suspicion of a developing pneumothorax. We present 
      our experience with an intra-procedural pneumothorax following EBUS-guided biopsy 
      and discuss the procedural considerations relevant to its prompt recognition and 
      management.
