TI  - Esophagus lyomyoma diagnosed with convex endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS).
PG  - 95-97
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2018.05.005 [doi]
AB  - Esophageal lyomyoma are rare benign tumors of the esophagus and they remain 
      usually undiagnosed until local compression symptoms occur in the esophagus. 
      Gastroscopy or esophageal ultrasonography (EUS) are usually the methods of choice 
      for diagnosis. Moreover; surgery is the solution for this entity. In our case we 
      present diagnosis of esophageal lyomyoma using convex probe endobronchial 
      ultrasound (EBUS) with a fine needle aspiration of 22G.
