TI  - Pulmonary Embolism as a Finding During Endobronchial Ultrasound: An Occasional 
      Occurrence or a New Element to Be Staged?
PG  - e20137
LID - 10.7759/cureus.20137 [doi]
LID - e20137
AB  - In this report, we describe two cases of lung cancer-related pulmonary embolism 
      (PE), both encountered while performing an endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS). We 
      propose EBUS as a diagnostic and confirmatory method for PE detection during the 
      staging of lung cancer.
