TI  - Endobronchial ultrasound EBUS--a new method for the diagnosis and staging of lung 
      cancer.
PG  - 23-5
AB  - In this paper we present a new method, endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS), which 
      appeared recently among the tools of the pulmonologist for the diagnosis and 
      staging of lung cancer. Endobronchial ultrasound transbronchial needle aspiration 
      (EBUS-TBNA) provides the opportunity for obtaining tissue samples required for 
      the histologic and cytologic diagnosis of lung cancer. The advantages of EBUS 
      have to be made popular as it is a minimally invasive method, safe, simple, fast, 
      also with a superior cost/benefit ratio compared to any previously used methods.
