TI  - Diagnosis of pulmonary embolism by endobronchial ultrasound.
PG  - 606-8
LID - 10.4103/0970-2113.168130 [doi]
AB  - This is a case report of a young 20-year-old male who was referred for an 
      endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) procedure to investigate a fever and a left hilar 
      lymph node and patchy pleural-based opacities seen on CT of the chest. During the 
      EBUS procedure besides the left hilar node, a large thrombus was noticed in the 
      main pulmonary artery and another one in the right pulmonary artery. EBUS proved 
      invaluable in making a diagnosis in an unsuspected case of pulmonary embolism.
