AB  - In the diagnosis of lung cancer, pulmonologists have several tools at their 
      disposal. From the tried and true convex probe endobronchial ultrasound 
      (EBUS)-guided transbronchial needle aspiration to robotic bronchoscopy for 
      peripheral lesions and new technology to unblind the biopsy tools, this article 
      elucidates and expounds on the tools currently available and being developed for 
      lung cancer diagnosis.
