TI  - 3-D endobronchial ultrasonography--a post mortem study.
PG  - 473-6
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasonography (EBUS) using balloon-embedded probes may cause 
      airway obstruction and requires a rapid scanning procedure. Three-dimensional 
      (3-D) postprocessing of sequential 2-D images may allow detailed studies on a 
      rapidly acquired image volume. We applied a 3-D reconstruction program on EBUS 
      recordings acquired with a radial-scanning probe during a controlled pullback 
      procedure in water-filled airways in five corpses. The aim was to acquire EBUS 
      images under optimized conditions and to test a 3-D software program for 
      postprocessing. Under post mortem conditions, 3-D images were obtained, allowing 
      any-plane imaging and measurements, application of different rendering and 
      visualization algorithms and merging of overlapping volumes.
