TI  - Asymptomatic silicone induced granulomatous disease diagnosed by endobronchial 
      ultrasound with real-time guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA).
PG  - 101102
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2020.101102 [doi]
LID - 101102
AB  - Silicone from ruptured breast implants can cause lung symptoms mimicking cancer. 
      The diagnosis may be established by transbronchial lung biopsy or surgery. We 
      report a case of asymptomatic silicone induced granulomatous reaction in the 
      lungs and mediastinal lymph nodes diagnosed with EBUS-TBNA. We conclude that this 
      differential diagnosis should be kept in mind even in an asymptomatic patients 
      and that EBUS-TBNA should be considered.
