TI  - RP EBUS as a guide for transbronchial pulmonary biopsy in the diagnosis of 
      organizing pneumonia.
PG  - 658
LID - 10.4081/mrm.2020.658 [doi]
LID - 658
AB  - Diffuse parenchymal lung diseases (DPLDs) include a wide variety of 
      manifestations characterized by different degrees of inflammation and fibrosis 
      with various patterns of secondary lobule alterations, such that the diagnosis 
      often requires histopathological confirmation in addition to clinical and 
      radiological data. Radial probe endobronchial ultrasonography (RP EBUS) can be 
      used as a guide for transbronchial pulmonary biopsy (TBPB) to obtain tissue 
      samples, and thus can be a useful tool in the diagnostic management of peripheral 
      pulmonary lesions. Organizing pneumonia (OP) is a particular type of DPLD 
      characterized by lung inflammation and scarring that obstruct the small airways 
      and air sacs of the lung. In this study, we describe how and when RP EBUS can be 
      used to guide TBPB and significantly help in the diagnosis of OP.
