TI  - A new mode of ventilation for interventional pulmonology. A case with EBUS-TBNA 
      and debulking.
PG  - 38-42
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2017.11.006 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is still underdiagnosed mainly due to lack of symptoms. Most patients 
      are diagnosed in a late stage where unfortunately only systematic therapy can be 
      applied. Fortunately in the last five years several novel therapies and 
      combinations have emerged. However; in certain situations local therapeutics 
      modalities have to be applied in order to solve emergency problems as in the case 
      that we will present. Convex-EBUS probe was used along with a novel method of 
      ventilation which keeps PCO(2) concentration satisfyingly low.
