OAB - The lung cancer biopsy specimens obtained by trans lung biopsy occasionally do 
      not contain cancer cells. It is a problem that there is a possibility that they 
      may not contain cancer cells. If the biopsy specimens contained no malignant 
      cells, there was a possibility that accurate genetic test would not be performed 
      and as a result, the correct molecular targeted drug would not be used. It is 
      important to investigate the proportion of biopsy specimens containing cancer 
      cells in total biopsy specimens. In this study, we showed the percentage of 
      specimens containing cancer cells in the total specimens was 79.0%. This result 
      should be considered to perform genetic test from biopsy specimens.
