TI  - [EBUS-guided cryobiopsy in the diagnosis of mediastinal lesions - step by step].
PG  - 420-426
LID - 10.1055/a-2295-5921 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) is 
      the gold standard in the diagnosis of mediastinal and hilar lesions. For certain 
      purposes, such as the diagnosis and subtyping of lymphoproliferative disorders or 
      molecular pathology, a larger amount of intact sample material is required. EBUS 
      cryobiopsy is a new and efficient tool for this purpose. As it is a new approach, 
      there is still no standardised workflow. In this review, we present the procedure 
      step by step as it is performed at the Ruhrlandklinik in Essen.
