TI  - Pulmonary Actinomyces graevenitzii Infection Diagnosed by Bronchoscopy using 
      Endobronchial Ultrasonography with a Guide Sheath.
PG  - 2547-2551
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.9799-17 [doi]
AB  - A 75-year-old man visited our hospital complaining of a low-grade fever, dry 
      cough, and chest abnormal shadow. Chest computed tomography revealed a nodule 
      with a cavity in the right upper lobe. Endobronchial ultrasonography (EBUS) of 
      the lesion suggested that the lesion was benign. Actinomyces graevenitzii was 
      cultured from the specimen obtained by bronchoscopy using endobronchial 
      ultrasonography with a guide sheath technique and was identified by 
      matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization time-of-flight mass spectrometry and 
      16S rRNA sequencing. The patient was treated with intravenous ampicillin; 
      subsequently, his condition improved. We believe that careful observation of EBUS 
      findings may be useful for the differential diagnosis.
FAU - Himeji, Daisuke
