TI  - The imaging of small pulmonary nodules.
PG  - 62-67
LID - 10.21037/tlcr.2017.02.02 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer death worldwide. The major goal in 
      lung cancer research is the improvement of long-term survival. Pulmonary nodules 
      have high clinical importance, they may not only prove to be an early 
      manifestation of lung cancer, but decide to choose the right therapy. This review 
      will introduce the development and current situation of several imaging 
      examination methods: computed tomography (CT), positron emission 
      tomography/computed tomography (PET/CT), endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS).
