TI  - Linear Endobronchial Ultrasound-Guided Microwave Ablation for Malignant Central 
      Airway Obstruction: A World-First Case.
PG  - e70384
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70384 [doi]
LID - e70384
AB  - We report the world's first case of malignant central airway obstruction (MCAO) 
      successfully treated with microwave ablation (MWA) under real-time linear 
      endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) guidance. A 72-year-old male with stage IVB lung 
      adenocarcinoma presented with severe dyspnea from a tumour causing 90% 
      obstruction of the right main bronchus. Using a linear EBUS scope, we performed 
      precise tumour mapping and positioned a MWA antenna with a 0.7 cm safety margin. 
      Controlled energy was delivered until an intratumoral temperature of 80°C was 
      reached, achieving immediate cytoreduction. The procedure resulted in 100% 
      luminal recanalization without requiring a stent. EBUS-guided MWA is a feasible, 
      safe, and highly effective technique for MCAO, offering unparalleled precision 
      and thermal control. This novel approach represents a significant advancement in 
      interventional pulmonology, enabling effective treatment of complex airway 
      tumours while enhancing patient safety.
