TI  - Endobronchial Ultrasound-Guided Transbronchial Needle Aspiration for Diagnosis 
      and Staging of Lung Cancer.
PG  - 111-123
LID - S0272-5231(17)30123-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.11.012 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS TBNA) is 
      fundamental to the diagnosis of lung cancer, as many patients present with more 
      advanced stages of lung cancer, with enlarged hilar and mediastinal lymph nodes. 
      It also represents a way to sample pulmonary masses directly to make the 
      diagnosis, whereby no other accessible tissue is present and the mass sits 
      adjacent to a large central airway. Very importantly also, EBUS TBNA is the 
      widely accepted first procedure in lung cancer staging. A combined procedure of 
      EUS TBNA can be performed to improve diagnostic accuracy.
