TI  - Major airway laceration secondary to endobronchial ultrasound transbronchial 
      lymph node biopsy.
PG  - 264-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181e6ff7d [doi]
AB  - A 48-year-old woman underwent complete mediastinal lymph node staging for 
      non-small-cell lung cancer. After convex endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS)-guided 
      transbronchial biopsy of the subcarinal lymph node station (station no. 7), it 
      was noted that a laceration had occurred in the left mainstem bronchus. The tear 
      occurred at the medial cartilaginous-membranous junction, seemed to be full 
      thickness into the mediastinum, and was approximately 1.5cm long. The cytologic 
      results of all lymph node biopsies were negative and the patient underwent right 
      upper and middle lobe bilobectomy 12 hours after the EBUS procedure. This is the 
      first report of a serious airway injury occurring during convex EBUS lymph node 
      biopsy.
