AB  - The article treats about utility of bronchoscopy and endoscopic biopsy techniques 
      in diagnosis of interstitial lung diseases (ILD). It describes macroscopic 
      changes visible in bronchoscopy in course of particular ILD and biopsy techniques 
      i.e. endobronchial biopsy (EBB), transbronchial lung biopsy (TBLB), 
      transbronchial "blind" needle aspiration (TBNA) and transbronchial needle 
      aspiration under endobronchial ultrasonography (EBUS-TBNA).
