VI  - 3
DP  - 2019
TI  - Intimal sarcoma of the pulmonary artery, a diagnostic enigma.
PG  - 32
LID - 10.21037/acr.2019.07.02 [doi]
LID - 32
AB  - Heart malignancies are rare and difficult to diagnose at early stage. Usually 
      they are discovered when they present disease symptoms. CT of the thorax with 
      contrast, MRI of the thorax, endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) or echocardiography 
      (transthoracic and/or transesophageal) and fluorodeoxyglucose positron emission 
      tomography-CT (FDG-PET-CT) can be used to diagnose this entity. We present a rare 
      heart sarcoma and our diagnostic algorithm.
