TI  - [Adult Middle Mediastinal Cystic Lymphangioma: Two Case Reports and Review of 
      Diagnostic and Therapeutic Challenges].
PG  - 385-390
LID - 10.1055/a-2831-6578 [doi]
AB  - Cystic lymphangiomas are rare (1% of all lymphangiomas, 0.7% of mediastinal 
      tumors), predominantly occurring in the anterior mediastinum. Middle mediastinal 
      localization is rare. They are typically asymptomatic and often found as an 
      incidental finding. EBUS-TBNA serves as a minimally invasive diagnostic and 
      occasionally therapeutic approach, while surgical resection remains the 
      definitive treatment with potential recurrence if resected incompletely. Herein, 
      we present two histologically confirmed middle mediastinal cases managed via 
      EBUS-TBNA aspiration and surgical resection, respectively.
