TI  - Airway manifestations of sarcoidosis in adolescents.
PG  - 2742-2744
LID - 10.1002/ppul.25002 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial sarcoid lesions have previously been described and visualized upon 
      bronchoscopy in adult patients with pulmonary sarcoid involvement. Endobronchial 
      ultrasound-guided transbronchial fine-needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) has come into 
      favor as the preferred method of diagnosis, but it remains a novel technique in 
      pediatric pulmonology. We describe the first two known cases of visualized 
      endobronchial sarcoid lesions in the pediatric population with pathological 
      confirmation of sarcoidosis with endobronchial and EBUS-TBNA biopsies.
