TI  - Enlarging mediastinal/hilar lymphadenopathy with calcification.
PG  - 212-3
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.451 [doi]
AB  - A 77-year-old man was referred to our hospital due to enlarging mediastinal/hilar 
      lymphadenopathy with calcification. Endobronchial ultrasound-guided 
      transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) and bone marrow aspiration were 
      performed. Subsequently, monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance 
      (MGUS) associated with mediastinal amyloidosis was diagnosed. We hereby report a 
      case in which EBUS-TBNA led to a successful diagnosis of amyloidosis.
