TI  - Concomitant Purulent Pericarditis and Pleuritis Due to Actinomyces odontolyticus 
      Following Endobronchial Biopsy for Pulmonary Sarcoidosis.
PG  - 1026-1031
LID - 10.1016/j.jaccas.2022.06.007 [doi]
AB  - The authors present a very rare case of bacterial purulent pericarditis due to 
      Actinomyces odontolyticus 2 weeks following an endobronchial ultrasound 
      bronchoscopy. On his presentation, he was in cardiac tamponade, for which he 
      underwent an emergent pericardiocentesis with purulent drainage. Similar 
      organisms grew in his left pleural effusion. (Level of Difficulty: 
      Intermediate.).
