TI  - Extensive Lymphadenopathy in an HIV-Negative Patient With Multidrug-Resistant 
      Tuberculosis.
PG  - e70480
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70480 [doi]
LID - e70480
AB  - Tuberculous lymphadenitis is generally more severe in patients with HIV 
      infection. We present an HIV-negative patient with multidrug-resistant 
      tuberculosis who developed severe, extensive lymphadenitis involving multiple 
      extrapulmonary regions. This clinical image highlights that marked lymph node 
      involvement may occur in HIV-negative patients presenting with pronounced 
      systemic symptoms.
