TI  - Lung cancer induced from chemotherapy a 20 years old case.
PG  - 32-34
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2018.03.013 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is diagnosed at a late stage although we have novel diagnostic tools. 
      The association of smoking and other environmental factors are well known. 
      However; there are cases where a malignancy is associated with previous radiation 
      treatment. There is an association between radiotherapy treatment and cancer 
      incidence. We present a case where lung cancer and laryngeal cancer was induced 
      20 years after radiation therapy of a hogkin lymphoma.
