TI  - Pulmonary mass with actinomyces infection mimicking malignancy: A case 
      illustrated.
PG  - e02264
LID - 10.1016/j.idcr.2025.e02264 [doi]
LID - e02264
AB  - We encountered a case of pulmonary actinomycosis diagnosed through bronchoscopy, 
      initially suspected as lung cancer originating from the bullae, and the PET-CT 
      findings did not rule out malignancy. Pulmonary actinomycosis is a rare lung 
      infection that often mimics cancer. Its anaerobic nature and prolonged culture 
      time make diagnosis challenging without strong clinical suspicion.
