TI  - A Case of Vanishing Bronchus Syndrome in a Non-lung Transplant Patient.
PG  - e50168
LID - 10.7759/cureus.50168 [doi]
LID - e50168
AB  - Vanishing bronchus syndrome (VBS) is the most severe form of bronchial stenosis. 
      It has been described as a complication following a lung transplant (LT). We 
      present a case of VBS in a patient with non-Hodgkin lymphoma in remission status 
      post chemotherapy and radiation therapy and no history of a lung transplant.
