TI  - CA 125 and TB.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2020-238199 [doi]
LID - e238199
AB  - We present two unusual presentations of extrapulmonary tuberculosis (EPTB) and 
      more specifically intra-abdominal tuberculosis (TB). These cases were initially 
      suspicious for ovarian cancer, presenting with non-specific symptoms, 
      ultrasound-confirmed ascites and elevated cancer antigen 125 tumour marker (CA 
      125). However, in both cases chest imaging demonstrated enlarged mediastinal 
      nodes amenable to endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle 
      aspiration (EBUS-TBNA), which confirmed the diagnosis of TB. Both cases were 
      successfully treated with quadruple TB therapy.
