TI  - Presentation of sarcoidosis as vocal cord palsy - A case series and review of 
      literature.
PG  - 367-370
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_612_24 [doi]
AB  - Sarcoidosis, is a complex multisystemic disease of unknown aetiology, which 
      manifests via a variety of symptoms frequently affecting multiple organs. Vocal 
      cord paralysis is rarely reported with Sarcoidosis. There have been very few case 
      report of patients presenting with vocal cord palsy due to mediastinal 
      lymphadenopathy causing compression of recurrent laryngeal nerve. We hereby 
      report a case series of 3 patients presenting with vocal cord palsy due to 
      recurrent laryngeal nerve compression by enlarged mediastinal lymph nodes due to 
      Sarcoidosis and also reviewed the supporting literature.
