TI  - Linear probe 19-gauge endobronchial ultrasound diagnosis of a benign chondroid 
      hamartoma.
PG  - 890
LID - 10.4081/monaldi.2018.890 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of a 68-year-old gentleman, found to have a right hilar soft 
      tissue mass whilst undergoing CT staging for prostate cancer. MRI imaging showed 
      a heterogenous, enhancing solid mass without evidence of fat content. A linear 
      probe endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration was 
      performed using a 19G needle. This confirmed the diagnosis of a benign chondroid 
      hamartoma, avoiding the need for more invasive surgical biopsy.
