TI  - Effect of rebiopsy methods and clinical features on T790M mutation after 
      first-line EGFR-TKI treatment failure.
PG  - 2475-2488
LID - 10.2217/fon-2021-0064 [doi]
AB  - Aim: This study investigated the association between clinical data and T790M 
      mutation in rebiopsy after EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitors (EGFR-TKIs) failure, 
      and explored the prognosis of T790M-positive patients. Methods: Patients with 
      non-small-cell lung cancer undergoing rebiopsy after first-generation TKI failure 
      were reviewed. Results & conclusion: Patients with brain metastases, negative 
      TP53, initial 19del and longer initial PFS had higher positive rate of T790M. The 
      median progression-free survival (PFS) of T790M-positive patients with cytology 
      and tissue rebiopsy were longer than patients with liquid rebiopsy. The median 
      PFS of T790M-positive patients rebiopsied by ordinary bronchoscope and 
      endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial lung biopsy with a guided sheath 
      (EBUS-GS-TBLB) were longer than that of the patients rebiopsied by EBUS 
      transbronchial needle aspiration (TBNA).
