TI  - Successful treatment of type B2 thymoma with steroid and radiotherapy.
PG  - e70006
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70006 [doi]
LID - e70006
AB  - An 86-year-old woman with leg edema and dyspnea on exertion was admitted to our 
      hospital. Chest computed tomography (CT) revealed a mass in the anterior 
      mediastinum with pericardial invasion. Histological examination with 
      endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) led 
      to the diagnosis of Masaoka stage IVa type B2 thymoma. For palliation, 
      radiotherapy (32 Gy/16 fractions) and prednisolone (30 mg/day) were administered 
      and tapered. After treatment, both the pericardial effusion and tumour size 
      decreased. Combination therapy with steroids and radiotherapy may be effective 
      for treating thymomas.
