TI  - Acute pneumothorax due to immunotherapy administration in non-small cell lung 
      cancer.
PG  - 101258
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2020.101258 [doi]
LID - 101258
AB  - Nowadays we have novel therapies for advanced stage non-small cell lung cancer. 
      Immunotherapy has been introduced in the market for several years and until now 
      its administration is mostly based on the programmed death-ligand 1. First line 
      treatment with immunotherapy can be administered alone if programmed death-ligand 
      1 expression is ≥ 50%. All therapies for advanced stage disease have advantages 
      and disadvantages, immunotherapy until now has presented mild adverse effects 
      when compared to chemotherapy. However; it is known to induce inflammatory 
      response to different tissues within the body. In our case acute pneumothorax was 
      induced after immunotherapy administration.
