TI  - Multimodality Image-Guided Embolization of Bronchial Artery Pseudoaneurysm in a 
      Patient With Aortopathy.
PG  - 721-726
LID - 10.1016/j.jaccas.2022.04.004 [doi]
AB  - A 59-year-old man received an incidental diagnosis of a 5-cm right para-aortic 
      mass that was initially thought to be of venous origin. Multimodality imaging 
      revealed a right bronchial artery pseudoaneurysm that was treated with 
      endovascular embolization. Bronchial artery pseudoaneurysms are extremely rare 
      and can be fatal if ruptured. (Level of Difficulty: Advanced.).
