TI  - The Diagnostic Challenge of Extrapulmonary Tuberculosis: Esophageal Perforation, 
      Mediastinitis, Pneumopericardium, and Pericardial Abscess Formation.
PG  - 266-270
LID - 10.1016/j.jaccas.2019.10.036 [doi]
AB  - We describe the case of extrapulmonary tuberculosis complicated by esophageal 
      perforation, pneumopericardium, and pericardial abscess formation. This case 
      illustrates the difficulty in diagnosing extrapulmonary tuberculosis, as the 
      occurrence of tuberculosis is rare in the developed world. The appropriate 
      treatment strategy and 6-month follow-up results are discussed. (Level of 
      Difficulty: Advanced.).
