TI  - Long term safety and visibility of a novel liquid fiducial marker for use in 
      image guided radiotherapy of non-small cell lung cancer.
PG  - 24-28
LID - 10.1016/j.ctro.2018.07.004 [doi]
AB  - Safety and clinical feasibility of injecting a novel liquid fiducial marker for 
      use in image guided radiotherapy in 15 patients with non-small cell lung cancer 
      are reported. No major safety or toxicity issues were encountered. Markers 
      present at start of radiotherapy remained visible in cone beam computed 
      tomography and fluoroscopy images throughout the treatment course and on computed 
      tomography images during follow-up (0-38 months). Marker volume reduction was 
      seen until 9 months after treatment, after which no further marker breakdown was 
      found. No post-treatment migration or marker related complications were found.
